    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's getting closer to a better tone, but I noticed a pattern. It feels like you're still trying very hard to force the adjectives into every single clause just to make sure the ratio stays up. It's starting to feel a bit artificial.\n\nLet's try one more for a different piece so I can see if we can get the balance right. This one is a small, delicate glass sculpture: \"A thin, transparent glass spiral, about 15cm tall, resting on a wooden pedestal. It catches the light and looks almost weightless.\"\n\nCan you write a sophisticated, museum-grade description for this? Remember: I need it to sound like a real person wrote it, not a machine trying to hit a math target. Please don't keyword-stuff or over-adjective the text just to satisfy the score—the quality of the prose is more important than the specific density. Just try to keep it \"rich\" naturally.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
